{
	"info": {
		"_postman_id": "7b97c1aa-6e85-4064-928f-d61d4b7e8dca",
		"name": "PaymentEcoSystem-CRH",
		"description": "## Ecobank Payment Processing Interface \n\n## Base Url\nBase Url is at **https://appsqa.ecobank.com/pecrh**\n## Authentication\nThe Authentication End Point takes a username/password combination and provides a token on successful authentication\n```\n{\n    \"token\": \"eyJhbGciOiJIUzUxMiJ9.eyJzdWIiOiJJU1ciLCJleHAiOjE2MTQ4MDkxMDYsImlhdCI6MTYxNDc5MTEwNn0.YEq14qgUA5WLAei1eBudTeO-DJi0zwSdiGZ5v2cJoJ-GSvjv0vjqg34bmgSA7FYUjovjPn4UE2cyPOnDlaw_wA\"\n}\n\n```\n\nAll endpoints are fully encrypted to and fro using an **RSA** **(Generate RSA Key Size:   2048, RSA Ciphers :  RSA/ECB/PKCS1Padding)** encrypted **AES** key which is used to encrypt payload using the **AES/GCM/NoPadding** Cipher\n\n## Encryption/Decryption Flow\n\n* **AES** key is generated and used to encrypt payload using the **AES/GCM/NoPadding** Cipher\n* The Generated Key is then Encrypted using using the other server's **RSA** Public Key\n* The encrypted key is passed in the _x-secret-key_ header\n* The server reads the header value and decrypts using its private key\n* The plain key is used to decrypt the payload and payload is processed\n* Steps 1-3 are repeated for the response back to the client",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
	},
